  <p>Since the inception of the NDA exam in 2006, the topic of Panchayati Raj has featured in roughly <span style="color: var(--warning);">12–15%</span> of the total polity questions. The most recurrent sub‑topic is the constitutional basis (73rd Amendment, Article 243) followed by the reservation norms for women and the three‑tier structure. In CDS papers, the focus shifts slightly towards the historical committees (Balwant Rai Mehta, Ashok Mehta) and the fiscal devolution percentages.</p>
